Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 27/9/2024

Yashin is an anime-themed card game bot for Discord. This Privacy Policy outlines what data we collect, how we use it, and your rights regarding that data. By using the bot, you agree to the terms outlined here.

1. Information We Collect
We collect minimal data to ensure the proper functioning of Yashin. This includes:

User ID and Server ID: Collected for in-game progress, leaderboards, and inventory management.
Interaction Data: Commands you use and responses from the bot, used for gameplay tracking and improvement.
We do not collect personal information such as names, emails, or any other personally identifiable information (PII).

2. How We Use the Information
The data we collect is used solely to provide and improve the bot's functionality:

To maintain your in-game progress (e.g., your card collection, in-game currency, etc.).
To provide a personalized experience across different servers.
To monitor and improve bot performance and functionality.
3. Data Sharing
We do not share or sell any collected data with third parties. The data is stored securely and is only accessible to the bot’s development team to ensure smooth operation and resolve any issues.

4. Data Retention
We retain your data as long as you continue to use Yashin. If you stop using the bot or remove it from a server, your data may be deleted after a reasonable period.

5. Your Rights
As a user, you have the right to:

Request deletion: You may request the deletion of your data at any time by contacting our support team.
Access your data: You may request access to the data we have stored about your account.
For data-related requests, contact us at [support@example.com] or through our support server.

6. Security
We take appropriate security measures to protect your data. However, please note that no method of transmission or storage over the internet is 100% secure. We strive to protect your data but cannot guarantee its absolute security.

7. Changes to this Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make significant changes, we will notify users via the bot's announcement channels or our support server.
